date,area,claimed,was_true,caught_by,lesson
日期,範圍,我當時的說法,實際情況,被什麼抓到,教訓
2026-08-27,Swift concurrency,"nonisolated(unsafe) on a local fixes a sending error","It does for a reference being passed along; not for a closure's type, nor for a value whose region holds isolated state","The same error reappearing at the same line, twice","Three encounters before the rule was clear. Annotate the type, not the local, when the region is the problem."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"A WinUI sweep can show almost nothing beyond launch","The desktop fallback photographs the window perfectly; P8's capture showed the scroll its action file performs","Actually opening the capture instead of reasoning about it","Look at the artefact before writing what it can prove."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"P4's gtk4 build failure is a regression","P4 is the WinUI escape-hatch app; canImport(WinUIBackend) is true even under -gtk4","Its WinUI build passing in the same run","A FAIL next to a PASS on the same app is a question, not a finding."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"P20 exits before the capture, so P20 has a defect","The wait was 14 s; P20's action file holds 16.8 s of sleeps","Its log had `replaying` and no `replayed`","When one item of twenty-four fails, suspect the harness's constant first."
2026-08-27,Tooling,"MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*' with tasklist //FI","tasklist needs the doubled slash and NO exclusion; taskkill needs the opposite","Every app reporting launch failure with its window on screen","Already written in memory. Reading it is not the same as checking it."
2026-08-27,Process,"A sed one-liner is fine for a two-line rename in a scratch file","It happened to be right","Noticing afterwards, not before","The rule says every file change goes through Edit. Convenience is exactly when it gets broken."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"Adding six targets to migratedToSwift6 after measuring four","Gtk had two errors on Windows and broke every gtk4 app build","A P8 build failing in the sweep, not a targeted build","Measure each target before listing it. The list is cheap to extend one name at a time."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"A typo guard on migratedToSwift6 is pure safety","It rejected GtkBackend on Windows, where SCUI_HOST_BACKENDS_ONLY deletes that target before the check","Its first real use","A guard that has never fired has never been tested."
2026-08-27,Audit,"ButtonStyle, LabelStyle, ShapeStyle and ToggleStyle are all absent","ToggleStyle has one declaration and ten references","Reading Toggle.swift for another reason","The grep was piped through head -10. Count, do not sample, when the claim is 'none'."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"One script can build and drive every app","The build gaps are idle time; the workstation locked itself out at the second app","The run itself","Split work by what it needs from the environment, not by what it is about."
2026-08-27,Swift generics,"Shadow `backend` with the cast result","The existential does not satisfy BaseAppBackend","Twenty conformance errors at once","A cast that narrows can also lose what the caller already had."
2026-08-27,Measurement,"eval getwindowgeometry --shell then eval getmouselocation --shell","The second overwrote X and Y, so the probe compared the cursor with itself","Every offset coming out 0,0","A clean null result from a probe is a reason to check the probe."
2026-08-27,Environment,"Awake can run however it likes","Its console window sat in the middle of the screen, over the desktop captures the WinUI pass depends on","Seeing it in a capture","A tool added to help the test is part of the test."
2026-08-26,Performance,"WSL is 3-4x faster than Windows for this project's builds","Windows is 3.3x faster for a full build; WSL is 9.5x faster for a no-op","A clean measurement of both","Two different questions were being answered by one number."
2026-08-26,Performance,"-gtk4 is slower because Gtk is a big module","130 s versus 123 s, 5% apart; the 118 s was mtime churn","Measuring instead of explaining","An explanation that arrives before the measurement usually survives it."
2026-08-26,UI testing,"P24 and P20 stop receiving clicks","The coordinates were measured on a capture the file's own earlier steps had invalidated","Retracting it twice before finding the pattern","A step that changes the layout must be the last step that uses that layout's coordinates."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"swift build -Xswiftc -swift-version -Xswiftc 6 measures the language mode","It is global, so it recompiled dependencies; all 17 errors were in swift-image-formats","None of the errors naming our own files","Size a per-target job with the per-target mechanism."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"SwiftCrossUI's one error needs a decision about the protocols","Two nonisolated keywords, and the cause was in BaseStubs rather than in the type the diagnostic named","Trying the fixes the diagnostic implied and watching them fail","The error names where it surfaced, not where it came from."
2026-08-27,Tooling,"csv2 -r emits tab-separated fields, so awk -F tab can pivot it","It emits CSV, quoting and all",Checking with od -c before trusting the pivot,The first version would have mis-parsed every row and produced a plausible empty matrix.
2026-08-27,Shell,grep -c prints 0 on no match so a || fallback is harmless,"It prints 0 AND exits 1, so both fired and the count became the two characters 0\n0",An integer comparison failing on a count,"A fallback for a case the tool already handles is a second answer, not a safety net."
2026-08-27,Review,"An agent reported my sweep evidence was invalid, and it sounded right","The sweep never used the broken function; same script, same grep, gave 16 ok on gtk4 and no line on WinUI",Checking whether sweep_drive.zsh references test_common.zsh at all -- it does not,A correct bug report can carry an incorrect consequence. Verify the consequence separately from the bug.
2026-08-27,Environment,The screen lock came from the sign-in timeout the user had already raised to 3 hours,It came from the screen saver: ScreenSaveTimeOut 600 with ScreenSaverIsSecure 1,Reading the registry instead of trusting the settings page,Windows has four independent things that lock a screen. Name which one before advising a change.
2026-08-27,UI testing,allowsHitTesting(false) does not block a click on GtkBackend -- P10 expects Hidden clicks 0 and gets 1,"1 is the working value. The modifier means the top layer does not take hits, so the click reaches the button below, which is what SwiftUI does. 0 is what a no-op produces",Replacing setHitTesting with a no-op and watching the counter fall to 0,A counter that moves is not automatically a failure. Establish which direction means working before filing it.
2026-08-27,Windows input,"Keyboard action files cannot run at all on Windows, so AttachThreadInput is needed",They already ran. The HWND_TOPMOST pin added after the task was filed had fixed it; P10 quit on Ctrl-Q with the new code and without it,Running the control -- the version without AttachThreadInput behaved identically,A task description is a claim with a date on it. Re-run the failure before writing the fix.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"The popover background after the fix is rgb(53,53,53), so the theme paints it now",The menu never opened. That was the window background -- the action file clicked before layout settled and missed silently,"Cropping the capture and looking at it, because the number was suspiciously tidy",A measurement of the wrong pixels reads exactly like a result. Confirm the thing being measured is on screen.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"Enabled and disabled WinUI buttons both have fill rgb(32,32,32)",The window moves between launches; those coordinates were outside it entirely,"Both fills matching, where the previous run had 45 and 42",Pixel coordinates expire when the window is relaunched. Locate the window in every capture before sampling it.
2026-08-28,Review,border: none plus box-shadow: none removes the GTK entry focus ring -- an agent sweep ranked this severity 5,"GTK 4 draws the ring with outline, which this backend never sets. Measured present at rgb(36,80,133), 196px wide",Measuring the focused and unfocused fields before repeating the claim,"A plausible mechanism is not a measurement. Check the mechanism, not only the symptom."
2026-08-28,Review,The TextEditor disabled state is hidden by its unconditional background: none -- from the same agent sweep,"The symptom was real, the cause was not. It was the forced foreground colour; fixing that alone restored the dimming, 255 to 145","A/B against HEAD by swapping the backend file, rather than reasoning from the report","A correct symptom can carry a wrong cause. Fix what the A/B shows, not what the report says."
2026-08-28,Measurement,"The popover change is unverifiable here -- Adwaita is identical before and after, so there is nothing to show","Under GTK_THEME=HighContrast the old code drew a dark rgb(44,44,44) menu on a white rgb(253,253,252) window, in the theme people pick because they need contrast",Trying the other theme instead of concluding from the default one,A no-op under the default configuration is not evidence of no effect. Vary the input the code actually branches on.
2026-08-28,Attribution,"Standing the GtkBackend isControl background down fixes #390, since disabled buttons come out distinct","The disabled-to-enabled gap survived both ways, 5 units versus 10. What the enforcement actually destroyed was the border",Measuring the two states instead of reading the screenshot,Do not attach a known issue to a change because the screenshot looks better.
2026-08-28,Review,"modelbutton is missing from the opacity: 0.5 disabled rule, so disabled menu items read as enabled","modelbutton IS missing and it does not matter -- GTK dims an insensitive menu item through its label colour without the rule. The real cause was the popover CSS forcing a flat colour over the theme, already fixed hours earlier","Building the instrument P20 never had, then A/B-ing it against the pre-fix backend",Two plausible causes for one symptom. The one that names a missing line of CSS is the more convincing and was the wrong one.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"Pre-fix menu labels measured 53,53,53 and 255,255,255 -- so the disabled item was BRIGHTER than the enabled one","Those rows were sampled from a window that had moved between launches. Read off the image, all three were 255,255,255",The numbers being impossible -- an enabled label darker than the menu background,Same window-moved error as twice earlier today. An impossible number is a gift; a merely surprising one is the danger.
2026-08-28,Tooling,"Tallied the coverage matrix by piping csv2 --json into Python, and read off 45 RUN / 13 BUILT per platform","The tally was of surrogate-escaped byte soup -- every emoji comparison failed, so the counts were of unrecognised strings. The file itself is valid UTF-8; od -c gives E2 9C 85 for the tick",The status names printing as surrogate escapes instead of RUN or BUILT,"Windows ACP here is 950 and Python 3.14 leaves UTF-8 mode off, so a piped script inherits the locale for stdin and stdout rather than the file encoding. PYTHONUTF8=1 fixes it -- but csv2 -contains --filter listed the same rows with no Python at all, so the bug came of reaching past the tool that was already correct."
2026-08-28,Tooling,"Counted the coverage matrix at 107 records, by grepping csv2 --json output for the substring fields","104. The opening meta line carries a fields key holding the FIELD count (10), so a substring grep matches it as well as every record -- an over-count of exactly one, which reads as an off-by-one in my own edit rather than a bad method. csv2 already emits records:104 in its trailing meta, and csv2 -r piped to wc -l agrees","The number failing to move by exactly 1 across a single append, then counting three ways","Do not count JSON Lines by grepping a key: the same key appeared at two levels meaning two different things. csv2 answers the question itself. Its --help describes --json in five words and mentions neither the meta lines nor the records count, so this is also a csv2 doc gap."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Scanned menu rows for a separator by flagging every row whose dominant colour changed, and read the result as a list of candidates","That flags every row containing text, because glyphs break the dominant-colour run. It buried the one row that mattered. Then the same scan on a second run reported rgb(53,53,53) rows that were the window background, because the window had moved and the fixed coordinates missed the popover entirely",The colour being the window background rather than anything in a menu -- and it was the fourth window-moved miss in two days,"Define the signal before scanning for it. A separator is a row whose dominant colour spans the FULL width AND differs from the background; locate the popover by its own colour first, never by coordinates from a previous run."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Measured P39 cell means and got saturation 0 and saturation 2.5 identical, then reported deltas around 20 for six effects","Impossible on its face -- opposite effects cannot share a mean. The sample boxes sat at different relative offsets INSIDE their cells, and the gradient is conic, so each offset sees a different mix of hues. Re-measured at identical offsets: five of six were delta exactly 0.0",Two effects with opposite meanings returning the same number,"Anchor a sample to the thing being measured, not to the screen. Locate the cell, then sample the same relative window inside every one."
2026-08-29,Measurement,Mean cell colour is enough to tell whether a visual effect was applied,"It cannot see a blur at all -- averaging is what a blur does, so the mean is preserved. GTK blur measured delta 2.3 by mean and would have been filed as a no-op; by text edge energy it is 53.21 -> 1.76, a 30x drop, and plainly applied","P39 own header saying the text is the only thing with edges, read after the number looked wrong","Choose the metric from what the effect DOES. A single metric that cannot distinguish applied from dropped is not a weak test, it is a wrong answer."
2026-08-29,Diagnosis,"GTK 4.22.4 cannot render a transformed widget at all -- filed as a platform defect after ruling out four causes, one of which was the renderer","There is no GL renderer on this machine to have ruled out. GTK cannot realize it (OpenGL requires Direct Composition) and silently falls back to software GskCairoRenderer, which is the thing that cannot draw a transform node. GDK_DEBUG=dcomp gets GskGLRenderer and every transform renders correctly, hotpink 47873 -> 0","Five GSK_RENDERER values returning byte-identical 47873 -- five renderers cannot agree to the pixel, so they were one renderer five times","A control that silently degrades to the thing it was meant to be compared against proves nothing. Verify the alternative was actually used, not merely requested."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Wrote the probe that re-enables the GTK transform, ran it, got 0 hotpink and nearly recorded that the bug was gone","The probe emitted matrix(..., 40px, 20px). CSS matrix() takes <number>, so px made the declaration invalid and GTK dropped it silently. Nothing was transformed and the tiles were still 90x57",Checking the tile geometry rather than trusting the count -- a probe that fails to apply looks exactly like a fixed bug,"When a test can pass for two reasons, one of them being that it never ran, measure the thing that distinguishes them every time."
2026-08-29,Tooling,"Put new backend code in a new file, Sources/GtkBackend/GtkBackend+GpuPreference.swift, and spent several builds debugging why the symbol was not found","The file was never compiled. Proven with a #error inside it that never fired, while edits to EXISTING files in the same directory took effect in the same build. Touching Package.swift to force a re-plan did not help. Moving the identical code into GtkBackend.swift compiled first time",The #error not firing -- the only test that separates not-compiled from compiles-but-wrong,"CAUSE STILL UNKNOWN, and recorded as unknown rather than guessed. Under testapp/compile.zsh a NEW .swift file under Sources/ may not enter the build; add code to an existing file, or verify with a temporary #error before debugging anything else."
2026-08-29,Diagnosis,"Deleting .build/debug.yaml did not make compile.zsh notice a new source file, so the cached build plan was ruled out","It was the right theory and the wrong directory. There are THREE work dirs -- .compile-work, .compile-work-gtk4, .compile-work-winui, one per backend -- and .gitignore documents them. The deletions hit .compile-work while -gtk4 builds in .compile-work-gtk4. Deleting the right one made the file compile immediately",Reading .gitignore for an unrelated reason and seeing the per-backend comment,"Ruling a theory out is a measurement too, and it fails the same way as any other: on the wrong target. Confirm the artefact being deleted is the one in use before concluding from its absence."
2026-08-29,Tooling,"Used taskkill //F //IM throughout, including inside a new zsh test script, having read the memory note that says taskkill needs the opposite slash treatment from tasklist","Under zsh it fails outright -- ERROR: Invalid argument/option - //F -- and the process SURVIVES. bash converts //F to /F and zsh does not, so the identical line works from the interactive shell and fails in a .zsh script. With stderr discarded it is completely silent, and the leftover GTK process then makes the next launch exit 0 with no window and no output","Four test cases reporting an empty log, then testing the kill directly instead of assuming it worked","tasklist wants the doubled slash, taskkill wants the single one. The memory said so and reading it was not the same as applying it -- the second time that exact sentence has been earned this week."
